+### Why the search tint is set before each frame and not on transcript changes
+
+The Kit parses a text view's Markdown after its text is set, and its
+rendered text, which highlight ranges index, changes only when that parse
+lands. A search run from the transcript change would index the previous
+parse. Before each frame the bar compares every hit view's rendered text
+with the one it last searched and searches only a view whose parse or
+emphasis changed, so a streaming hit is painted again per landed parse and
+an idle frame searches nothing. With the bar closed the frame does no work.
+
+### Why the current hit's tint is translucent
+
+The reference paints the current hit's words in the solid primary color and
+turns their text to the primary foreground. A Kit range highlight paints a
+background and leaves the text's own color, which the solid primary would
+make unreadable in some themes. The current hit takes the primary color at
+60 %, every other hit at the reference's 30 %.
+
+### Why the header menu decides its lines at each draw
+
+The session row menu keeps the lines it opened with and is rebuilt when an
+answer it waits for arrives. The header menu has one session and eight
+lines, so it reads the session's state at each draw and at each key press:
+an AI rename check that answers, a turn that starts or a rename that
+settles shows without a rebuild hook, and an item that stopped being
+offered cannot run. The highlight is kept by action, so it survives a line
+appearing or leaving.
+
